    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "A bicycle wheel of radius 36 cm turns through an angle of $\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$ radians in 0.16 seconds. At what speed is the bicycle being ridden, in metres per minute? Answer in exact form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$90\\pi\\text{ metres/min}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}r&=0.36\\text{ m}\\\\l&=r\\theta\\\\l&=0.36\\times\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\\\l&=0.24\\pi\\text{ m}\\\\t&=\\frac{0.16}{60}\\text{ min}\\end{align*}$$\nSpeed = distance ÷ time.\n$$\\begin{align*}v&=\\frac{0.36\\times\\frac{2\\pi}{3}}{\\frac{0.16}{60}}\\\\v&=90\\pi\\text{ metres/min}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
